# res://dialogue/chapter2_intro.dialogue
# chapter 2 opening: the dream at the door, then the wake onto the pannable CG.
# game states are [the intro overlay, the wake CG layer]. shake / shake_stop / cut_to_black /
# hide_visual_layers / wake_blink resolve on the overlay; stage_wake_cg / pan / reveal resolve
# on the wake layer.
# opening lines are speaker-less on purpose: the balloon hides the nameplate when the
# character is empty.

import "res://dialogue/layla_chapter_1.dialogue" as layla_ch1

~ start
Standing at the door.
A tall shadow.
His back turned against you.
What was his name again?
Name...
What was yours?
Maybe he'll call it out.
Maybe you should ask him where he's headed.
- Where are you going? => voice

~ voice
???: Huh?
???: Fiona.
???: You're not supposed to be up right now.
???: Go, sleep.
???: You need to sleep, Fiona.

# finite long shake + explicit stop. a persistent shake(-1) would be auto-cancelled by the
# overlay's got_dialogue handler one line in, now that the balloon goes through
# begin_conversation(). the 60s timer is never reached.
do shake(60.0, 3.0)
???: Sleep, Fiona.
???: Sleep, Fiona.
???: Sleep, Fiona.
do shake_stop()

???: Wake up.

# the hand-off happens UNDER the black: the overlay's opaque layers go dark and the wake CG
# is staged on layer 70 beneath the overlay's 75, so the eyelid opens straight onto it.
do cut_to_black(0.9)
do hide_visual_layers()
do stage_wake_cg()
do wake_blink(1.0)

Boobs: Fiona! You spent the last night working, didn't you?
Fiona: Huh!? Boobs?
Layla: Boobs?

do pan()
Layla: What are you talking about?

do reveal()
Layla: Hey. Earth to Fiona.

# the reveal tween may still be running under that line: let it land, then fade the wake
# CG out onto the level. wait_for_pan and fade_out resolve on the wake layer through
# extra_game_states, same as stage_wake_cg / pan / reveal above. from here the LEVEL is
# the backdrop — no background or CG goes up, and the darken backdrop is still hidden
# from hide_visual_layers earlier.
do wait_for_pan()
do fade_out(0.7)

# dim the live level so the sprites read on top of it. the overlay's dialogue-ended
# fade already tweens this back to 0, so nothing needs to clear it before END.
do set_backdrop_darkness(0.5, 0.4)
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
# the real post-wake conversation lives in layla_chapter_1.dialogue so the same lines
# back the in-world talk_to verb. jump into it; it sets layla_post_wake_intro_seen and
# ends the dialogue itself.
=> layla_ch1/post_wake_intro
